[about]
Title=04 - Open and Move Through a Database
Intro=Opening JobTrail, the first template, and moving through it: what a row says, what a cell says, the next table, and then the menus, which name every key as you arrow through them. This walk assumes walks one to three.
Setup=DbDo is open and no database is open yet.
Homework=Open JobTrail, arrow through it, and read the File and Edit menus to the end.

[step]

Say=Each row is one job I am after: employer, title, and where it stands.
Key=DownArrow
Hear=Example Widgets Company (sample employer) Accessibility Analyst interviewing, 2 of 4
Note=That one is the job I want most.

[step]

Say=It is a grid. Down and Up move between records; Left and Right between fields.
Key=RightArrow
Hear=Accessibility Analyst

[step]

Say=Shift plus C, Say Cell -- C for Cell. The field I am on, and its value.
Key=Shift+C
Hear=title, Accessibility Analyst
Note=Every Shift and letter asks a question, and none changes anything.

[step]

Say=Down keeps the field, so I can compare one field down the list.
Key=DownArrow
Hear=Digital Services Assistant

[step]

Say=My reader's say-line key reads the whole row again. Shift plus Z, Say Status, gives the summary. H for Here.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=status, jobs row 3 of 4, sort employer

[step]

Say=Control plus Page Down moves to the next table. JobTrail gives me five: actions, contacts, docs, jobs and stories.
Key=Control+PageDown
Hear=JobTrail dot d b, stories
Hear=Records list view
Note=Two more tables hold DbDo's own pick lists and links. It keeps those out of the way.

[step]

Say=Alt opens the menu bar. Each menu's first letter opens it directly.
Key=Alt
Hear=Menu bar
Hear=File, F
Note=File, Edit, Navigate, Query, Misc, Window, Help. Every letter differs.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow opens File. Each item gives its key, then its letter.
Key=DownArrow
Hear=New Database..., N

[step]

Say=Down Arrow moves to the next item, and each one says its letter last.
Key=DownArrow
Hear=Add Table..., A

[step]

Say=Down Arrow again, and this one has a key as well as a letter.
Key=DownArrow
Hear=Open Database..., Control+O, O
Note=The key works from anywhere. The letter works while the menu is open. They match whenever the key has a letter.

[step]

Say=A few menus hold a submenu for a large or rarely used group. Edit, B for Bulk Marking, is one. Right Arrow goes in; Left Arrow comes back.
Key=Escape
Hear=Leaving menus
Note=The others: Query, S for Say, Misc, T for Tools, and Help, M for More Documents. None goes deeper than one level.

[step]

Say=DbDo can keep several tables open, each in its own window -- the multiple document interface. Control plus Tab moves among DbDo windows.
Key=Control+Tab
Hear=JobTrail dot d b, actions
Hear=Records list view
Note=Control plus Shift plus T opens a table in a new window. Control plus F4 closes one.

[step]

Say=F1 is help: the guide. Shift plus F1 is the history, Control plus F1 describes the next key I press.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer On
Note=Help also holds the ReadMe, Hotkeys, the FAQ, and Play Tutorials.

[step]

Say=F11 is Elevate Version -- elevate sounds like eleven. It checks for a newer DbDo.
Key=F11
Hear=Elevate Version dialog
Note=Nothing downloads without asking.

[step]

Say=Home and End reach the first and last field of the row; Control plus Home and Control plus End the first and last record; Page Up and Page Down move a screen of records at a time.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Typing a letter jumps to the first record whose first column starts with it, in the current order; so a sorted list is reached by its first letters, as a file list is.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Control plus G, Go to Record, takes a number, for when you know the row.
Key=Control+G
Hear=Go to Record dialog, Row: edit

[step]

Say=Escape. Everything in this walk works the same in every table and every template: the grid is the grid.
Key=Escape
Hear=JobTrail jobs

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Shift plus C.
Key=
Hear=Say Cell

[step]

Say=Shift plus Z.
Key=
Hear=Say Status

[step]

Say=Control plus Tab.
Key=
Hear=Next Window

[step]

Say=Control plus F1.
Key=
Hear=Key Describer Toggle
